  "notes": "Trimmed PDF has 8 pages. Governmental funds are cash basis (p3 total column); business-type funds (water, sewer, golf) are accrual basis, so business_type measure is net position and proprietary is null (cash flow statement p6 not recorded because basis is cash). Governmental total revenues 1,381,520 includes Transfers In 2,537 and total expenditures 1,510,716 includes Transfers Out 2,537; both are in transfers_in/out, not receipts/disbursements. Capital Grants and Contributions blank in total column. Business-type printed no single totals (operating and nonoperating shown separately); totals computed. Balance sheet uses p1 government-wide statement (governmental cash basis + business accrual) Total column; zero lines omitted. Budget schedules p7-p8 are General and Special (street) funds; the General Fund 'Transfer in' 7,744 equals insurance proceeds on p3 and is included in printed total revenues. Keno Fund has no budget schedule in the trimmed pages. Recheck: Charges for Services split by fund column (General 367,745 charges for services; Keno Fund 44,252 keno/lottery), p3. Read pages 1-8 of 8.",
